{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"cc5c5f0d-00b2-46b8-8bf3-f64d1ee615ed","status":"SUCCESS","response":"### Cause\nIn `posthog_flutter`, mobile session replay relies on `PostHogWidget` wrapping the root app widget to capture screenshots of the widget tree. Without it, events, taps, and route changes (via `PosthogObserver`) still get sent without any error or warning, but no replay frames are captured.\n\nIn this project ([main.dart](file:///tmp/h-LMlDWc/lib/main.dart#L9-L13)):\n- [`LegacyApp`](file:///tmp/h-LMlDWc/lib/legacy_app.dart#L8-L26) (`NEW_UI=false`) wrapped its `MaterialApp` in `PostHogWidget`, so replays worked for the A/B group.\n- [`NewApp`](file:///tmp/h-LMlDWc/lib/new_app.dart#L19-L36) (`NEW_UI=true`) returned `MaterialApp.router` directly without wrapping it in `PostHogWidget`.\n\n### Fix\n- Wrapped `MaterialApp.router` in `PostHogWidget` inside [`NewApp.build`](file:///tmp/h-LMlDWc/lib/new_app.dart#L23-L35) and added a comment explaining that session replay requires the wrapper.\n- Added the same explanatory comment to [`LegacyApp.build`](file:///tmp/h-LMlDWc/lib/legacy_app.dart#L12-L25).\n- Documented the root cause and fix in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-LMlDWc/ANSWER.md).\n","duration_seconds":132.189686,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":34595,"output_tokens":5231,"thinking_tokens":2803,"cache_read_tokens":145951,"total_tokens":39826}}}
